+## 9. Post-submit edits of this row (`RequestActionsHandler.js`)
+
+Two Forms functions change an `Initial Requests` row after `submitInitialRequest`; both authorise by the **real session
+principal** (`Actor.principal()`, HR/IT/Admin via `AccessControlService.getUserRolePayload`) and write the `Audit Log`.
+Neither sends email or changes the step.
+
+| Function | Alias | Column written | Extra trail | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `updateHireDate(workflowId, 'yyyy-MM-dd')` | `n8n_updateHireDate` | 6 / Hire Date | `Audit Log` `UPDATE_HIRE_DATE`; `syncWorkflowState` (Dashboard_View has a Hire Date column) | pre-existing |
+| `updatePreferredName(workflowId, preferredName)` *(added 2026-09-17)* | `n8n_updatePreferredName(actor, workflowId, preferredName)` — wrapper `n8n/29_Forms_UpdatePreferredName.json` | 13 / Preferred Name (found **by header name**, like `updateHireDate`) | `Form Edit Log` row (`Form Type = Initial Request`, `Changed By = Actor.email()`, `Changes = col14: [old] → [new]`); `Audit Log` `UPDATE_PREFERRED_NAME` (User = principal, Detail `"old" → "new" (by <actor label>)`); Raw Log event `kind=request.updated`, `source=updatePreferredName`, payload `{ field:'preferredName', previous, value }` | value trimmed; rejects empty, leading `= + - @` (same rule as `validateRequiredFields`), > 100 chars, and a workflow whose `Workflows.Status` is `Cancelled`; **idempotent** — same value → `{ success:true, changed:false }` with no writes; no `syncWorkflowState` (Dashboard_View has no Preferred Name column) |
+
+Consumers of col 13 that therefore see the new value with no further action: `getWorkflowContext` (`EmailUtils.js:345` →
+email templates print `First (Preferred) Last`, `EmailTemplates.js:186`), `getIDSetupRequestData` (`IDSetup.js:78`),
+`getRequestDetails().requestData` (`ReferenceDataService.js:275`, header-keyed `Preferred Name`), `RequestHeader.html:105`,
+and the IT Confirmation prefill (`InitialRequest.html:729`). Caveat: an `it_confirmation` submit writes `formData.preferredName`
+back into col 13 (`ITConfirmationHandler.js:76`), so an n8n `it_confirmation` payload carrying a stale/blank `preferredName`
+would overwrite an HR edit — the UI path is safe because it prefills from the sheet.
+
+Alias envelope: `ok` → `result { success, changed, workflowId, preferredName, previousPreferredName, message }`;
+`E_VALIDATION` (missing/blank/formula-leading, `fields[]`), `E_NOT_FOUND` ("Workflow not found in Initial Requests" — TERM_ /
+CHANGE_ ids), `E_UPSTREAM` (Cancelled, too long), `E_FORBIDDEN` (principal not HR/IT/Admin; `error.principal`).
